      "problem": "Given that $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(0.65),$ compute $P(X = 0).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273447/assets/d621fedbca6841667351c25293baedfd426622fd6c6d188b5c840d6bf944d855.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(0.65),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273447/assets/202f19053a9b32640b703d8d3923992f4cb9e4e7ccf5c0de5d6533cabb0437fe.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X = 0) = f(0) = 0.35.\n$$",
